+# Chief Command — Session Handoff, 2026-07-21
+
+**Read this first, then `docs/TODO.md`.** The live open todos are in the DATABASE now
+(Projects tab, and pinned to the bottom of the terminal) — this doc explains the state
+they're in.
+
+---
+
+## TL;DR
+
+**#10 (the review panel) is DONE and PUSHED.** **#11 (the gatekeeper) is BUILT but NOT
+PUSHED** — it is committed locally at `66ad8a2` and 19 pre-existing tests still assert
+the old, laxer rules it changes. That is the first job of the next session.
+
+- Live app: `.venv/bin/python harness/server.py` → http://localhost:8787
+- Tests: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest harness/tests/ -q` → **166 pass, 19 fail** (all 19
+  are old tests encoding the pre-fix world — see below)
+- Migrations applied to the live DB: `001`–`007`
+- `main` is pushed through `3517c17`. `66ad8a2` is local only, deliberately.
+
+---
+
+## What got done
+
+### #10 — the full review panel (pushed, `3517c17`)
+
+Before: dispatch ran ONE reviewer, and "at least two different model families must
+agree" lived in a config file that nothing enforced.
+
+Now: reviewers run **in parallel against one frozen version**; the **database itself**
+refuses to complete a job unless enough genuinely different model families passed *that
+exact version*; a reviewer that was capped out, switched off or crashed is **written
+down as not having participated** and can never count as approval; money is reserved
+before a paid reviewer is called; and if the panel can't reach the floor, the work waits.
+
+Proved live twice: the free local model built something, Claude and GPT reviewed the
+same version side by side, the job completed, Grok logged as sitting out.
+
+Reviewers found eight real defects in it, including one that would have certified work
+nobody reviewed and one where a broken login would have permanently condemned good code.
+All fixed with regression tests.
+
+### #11 — the gatekeeper (built, NOT pushed, `66ad8a2`)
+
+`harness/gatekeeper.py`. Three verbs — merge, deploy, spend — and no fourth. Agents ask;
+it re-reads the record itself rather than believing the request. `dispatch.ship()`, which
+was one import away from every agent, is gone.
+
+Reviewers hit it hard and found more, all fixed — most seriously that **merge merged
+whatever the branch currently pointed at, never checking it was the code that had been
+reviewed**. Build v1, get it approved, push v2, ask to merge: v2 went in. It now refuses
+unless the branch tip *is* the reviewed version, and the record decides before git is
+touched at all.
+
+### Migration 007 — two holes under #10, found after it was pushed
+
+1. **A job with no requirements had no requirements to fail.** Both completion guards
+   only fired when the requirement counts were above zero, and they default to zero. A
+   job created outside dispatch went straight to done with no reviews at all.
+2. **The builder's own family counted toward "different minds."** A GPT seat could build
+   it, a GPT seat could pass it, and that counted as one of the two required families.
+   Same-family review is still *allowed* (deliberate earlier decision, and banning it
+   outright would deadlock a Claude-built job) — it just no longer counts toward
+   diversity.
+
+---
+
+## ⚠️ PICK UP HERE
+
+1. **Fix the 19 failing tests.** They are not regressions — they are old tests that
+   assert the behaviour migration 007 deliberately changed (jobs completing with zero
+   required reviews; the builder's own family counting toward the floor; `dispatch.ship`
+   still working). Each needs updating to the new rules. `test_jobs.py`,
+   `test_review_version_binding.py`, `test_sol_attacks.py`, `test_sol_round2.py`,
+   `test_gatekeeper.py`, `test_dispatch_executor.py`.
+2. **Re-run the reviewers on the whole of `66ad8a2`**, then push. It has NOT had a clean
+   review pass since the last round of fixes.
+3. **Build the Grok reviewer connection.** Neill rotated the xAI key today, so Grok can
+   come back as a genuine third model family — but `harness/gauntlet.py` has no runner
+   for the `xai` provider yet, and the seat is still `disabled = true` in
+   `harness/config/seats.toml`. Flip both together.
+4. Then: **#13 safety rails**, **#12 streaming Chief into voice**.
+
+---
+
+## Process note, on the record
+
+**I pushed #10 before all three reviewers had reported.** Two of three had come back
+clean; I pushed on that and the third — the cross-model one — then found two critical
+holes in what had already gone up (both fixed here, in migration 007). AGENTS.md rule 8
+says reviews before pushes, and "reviews" means all of them. That is why `66ad8a2` is
+sitting unpushed rather than following the same pattern twice.
+
+---
+
+## 🔴 NEILL'S TODOS
+
+Done today: ✅ xAI key rotated · ✅ OpenAI key rotated · ✅ Grok ruled out of the medical
+repo (permanent decision, recorded in `seats.toml`) · ✅ pm2 auto-runners deleted ·
+✅ leftover public tunnel config killed.
+
+Still open:
+- [ ] **Rotate the Anthropic key** — found live in the old v1 config.
+- [ ] **Turn on GitHub branch protection for `main`** (~5 min). Still the single
+      highest-leverage safety item in the project — it is enforced on GitHub's servers,
+      where nothing on this Mac can argue past it.
+- [ ] **Get production credentials off this machine.**
+
+### The "hole in the wall"
+
+The gatekeeper is a **door**. Every agent still runs as Neill and can open the database
+file directly, so a determined process could walk around it. The door is real; the wall
+isn't built. Three things close it, in order of value:
+
+1. **Branch protection** (above) — the only wall not on this machine.
+2. **Credentials off the machine** — the real defence against a prompt-injected agent.
+3. **A separate macOS account for the agents**, owning nothing, reaching the records only
+   through the gatekeeper. ~1 hour, needs his password once. **Not worth doing until 1
+   and 2 are done.**
+
+This limitation is stated plainly in `gatekeeper.py`'s own docstring, on purpose — a
+gatekeeper everyone believes in but that doesn't hold is worse than none.
+
+---
+
+## Where the todos live now
+
+`harness/db/chief.db`, table `todos`. Three places read it:
+- the app's **Projects** tab,
+- the **terminal status line** (`~/.claude/statusline-chief.sh`, wired into
+  `~/.claude/settings.json` — survives new windows and context clears),
+- and any session that reads this file.
+
+One list, shown three ways. They cannot drift.
+
+---
+
+## Key files
+
+| File | What |
+|---|---|
+| `harness/gauntlet.py` | The review panel. Parallel, one frozen version, fails closed. |
+| `harness/gatekeeper.py` | Merge / deploy / spend. The only holder. **Unpushed.** |
+| `harness/executor.py` | The worker. Builds in an isolated copy, parks for review. |
+| `harness/dispatch.py` | Records the job, stamps the panel requirements, refuses early. |
+| `harness/db/schema.sql` | The source of truth. Every guard is a trigger here. |
+| `harness/db/migrations/` | `001`–`007`. The live DB only ever advances through these. |
+| `docs/gatekeeper-task11-spec.md` | The #11 design, including the staged wall. |
