+# Chief Command — Session Handoff, 2026-08-27
+
+**Read this first, then `docs/TODO.md`.** Open todos for Codex live in
+`docs/gpt/GPT_TASK_QUEUE.md`; owner todos are in the database (Projects tab).
+
+## TL;DR
+
+- **The gatekeeper (#11) is finished, six-reviewer-reviewed, fixed, and pushed.** Every
+  reviewer's finding was either fixed or queued (below). 202 tests pass.
+- **Grok is the third mind on the review panel.** Plain HTTP runner, key from the
+  environment, only ever sends the bundle it is handed. Proved live: it failed a wrong
+  snippet and passed a right one. The seat is metered (that is what the runner calls —
+  the SuperGrok subscription covers the app, NOT the API) so its $1/day cap binds.
+- **Codex has its own lane now** (`docs/gpt/`, `scripts/`): tracked task queue and
+  worklog, a 4-seat GPT gauntlet that checks the working tree after every seat, and a
+  reviewer marker + pre-push tripwire. `./scripts/install-hooks.sh` once per clone.
+- **Owner said: "I don't really want to build a ton on this right now… let's chill and
+  talk."** Do not start big builds without a conversation. The one design conversation
+  he asked for is below.
+
+## What got done
+
+1. 19 stale tests updated to migration 007's rules (no guard weakened).
+2. Grok reviewer runner + seat enabled + live DB re-synced.
+3. Six-reviewer pass (5 Claude + Glass) over everything unpushed → fixes:
+   - token file can't fail open; merge merges the verified SHA under the lock;
+     spend grants logged; job-scoped approval needs that job; bogus job ids can't
+     lose a refusal; grants show as 'done'; transaction always unwound; 'voice' spend.
+   - worker commits its output on `job/<id>` so `head_version` is a real commit →
+     merge proved against a real git repo (grant + refuse-when-moved).
+   - grok metered, rations reach the DB, missing key excludes at the door, empty/cut
+     reply is a skip, family counts exclude the author everywhere.
+4. Found and removed a stale `core.hooksPath` pointing at a Desktop folder from before
+   the repo moved — **no git hook had fired in this repo for weeks.**
+
+## Still open (queued for Codex, in priority order — see the queue for detail)
+
+1. **Record what Grok spends** (the runner throws the usage block away).
+2. **A local "what have we used" reader** for the Claude/Codex subscriptions (both
+   leave per-session token counts on disk; Codex even records % of weekly limit used).
+3. **Pin grok-4.6** (xAI's own pick for code, newest, same price) + a no-`latest` test.
+4. **Wire `gatekeeper.merge` into the flow — nothing calls it yet.** Today nothing can
+   move a job to `shipped`. Needs a tester verdict too (schema guard 6).
+5. Drain the body on early HTTP refusals. 6. Merge holds a write txn across `git merge`.
+
+Not queued, noted: `_note`/`events` vs `gate_log` overlap; `xai` error bodies land
+unredacted in events (key never appears in a body today); gate_log's append-only
+trigger makes any job it references undeletable (accepted).
+
+## The conversation the owner asked for
+
+He asked: *how is this set up, why is there so much waiting, is there a better way?*
+Answer given (and he should be walked through it again when he's ready):
+
+- The mouth is Grok voice ($3/hr metered). **Chief is GPT-5.6-sol via Codex — a deep
+  reasoning model sitting in the conversational path**, ~13s to first token. The
+  streaming Chief (`chief_live.py`, ~1.4s) exists and is not connected (#12). That is
+  the waiting.
+- His $20 Grok sub does not feed the harness at all (API is billed separately).
+- Better way = finish the design, not change it: (1) connect streaming Chief to voice;
+  (2) fast lane / slow lane — quick answers on a fast non-reasoning model (Grok 4.6 is
+  ~5× faster to first token than GPT-5.6-sol), deep specs in the background;
+  (3) his requested **"favor Claude / Codex / Grok" dial** is the knob that picks who
+  sits in the fast lane and who builds. Fold "check usage" + "favor" into one spec.
+- Grok research (2026-08-27): Grok 4.6 is fast and cheap, mid-pack on hard agentic
+  benchmarks (65.9% DeepSWE vs GPT-5.6 73.0% / Fable 5 70.0%). Right role: reviewer +
+  cheap overnight builder. **Never the Grok Build CLI** — the July repo-upload story
+  was confirmed by xAI; API-only is the rule. Pin exact model ids, never `-latest`.
+
+## Owner's todos (unchanged)
+- Rotate the Anthropic key · turn on GitHub branch protection for `main` (the only
+  wall not on this machine) · get production credentials off this machine.
