   250	    -- THE VERSION UNDER REVIEW (Sol build gate 3, 2026-07-20). The exact content
   251	    -- hash the builder is putting forward — a git commit id. Reviews bind to this:
   252	    -- a verdict only counts toward completion while its reviewed_version matches.
   253	    -- The moment the builder changes the code, this changes, and every earlier
   254	    -- approval silently stops counting. Sol called the alternative the most
   255	    -- dangerous flaw in the system: "believable green checks on code nobody
   256	    -- reviewed." The gatekeeper's job at push time is to verify the code leaving
   257	    -- the building IS this hash — the DB proves the chain, git proves the content.
   258	    head_version  TEXT,
   259	
   260	    -- 'done'    = the gauntlet passed. The machine is satisfied.
   261	    -- 'shipped' = NEILL said it works on his device. Only he can move this.
   262	    -- These are NOT the same thing, and conflating them is how agents launder
   263	    -- confidence. From Chief's memory, learned the hard way:
   264	    --     "Chief must NEVER say 'shipped' unless Neill has confirmed it works on
   265	    --      his device. 'Shipped' is reserved for Neill-confirmed-working."
   266	    -- That rule now lives here instead of in a prompt.
   267	    status        TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'todo'
   268	                  CHECK (status IN ('todo', 'in_progress', 'review', 'done',
